{"title":"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Partridge family pays each of their five children a weekly allowance. The average allowance for each of the three younger children is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f9b76b8f6db99961a78ece506186b6bfb5eb00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The two older children each receive an average allowance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7ec7d697f60d96631c5c2a96f736d69a4c77b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />. The total amount of allowance money paid per week is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca94d2bba9fef66518dba977188b1612f564d1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\$50 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\$52.50 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\$105 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\$21 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\$55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"511\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the averages, we can first find the total money per week from the first group of children and the second group of children, and then add these together.\n</p><p>Because the average of the allowance of the first group of children is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f9b76b8f6db99961a78ece506186b6bfb5eb00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> children, the total amount of money earned per week is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d34fce301775b8b0e23c939b6476f7cfb853b86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$8 \\times 3 = \\$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Because the average of the allowance of the second group of children is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7ec7d697f60d96631c5c2a96f736d69a4c77b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> children, the total amount of money earned per week for the second group of children is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49bd56b0d2e6e057138d157fb419c8be336e9b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$13 \\times 2 = \\$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The total amount of money for all of the children is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4db2a821750b7dbd809779ad7ec78a38e3dd3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$24 + \\$26 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } \\$50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"177\" height=\"31\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat\">1999 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>